## Main changes

- Removed the fake Auto Ways candidate, invented vehicle ID and customer-facing K-Type.
- A normal plate search without a configured provider returns `WAITING FOR PLATE PROVIDER` with zero candidates.
- Multiple-candidate behavior is now a separate neutral `DEMO CANNED RESULT — no external call` endpoint; candidates are ENGINE level at most and carry no external ID/K-Type.
- vPIC is the only tested VIN source shown in the demo trace and remains BASIC.
- Provider matrix separates tested evidence, documented capability, waiting/access state, configuration state and research-only material.
- Removed static positive/negative fitment claims. All demo products require compatibility confirmation until a trusted FitmentProvider evaluates the selected vehicle/product pair.
- Replaced misleading real-looking references with explicit synthetic `SAMPLE-*` values.
- Orders accept product ID + quantity only; FastAPI calculates prices and totals from server catalogue data.
- Removed client-specific conflict logic. Normalization/conflict checks are generic; the canned conflict is isolated demo data.
- Added HTTP Basic prototype role boundaries for customer/garage and admin/operations routes; garage is user scoped and deduplicated.
- Fixed saved vehicle year parsing.
- `DEMO_MODE` defaults to false and requires explicit opt-in.
- Removed the client's plate from the homepage and used `AB-12-CD` as a neutral placeholder.
- Marked delivery timing `ESTIMATIVA DEMO`; empty cart has zero shipping and total.
- Split VIN and plate traces. VIN includes vPIC; plate trace contains only plate-capable candidates plus manual fallback.
- Unfinished admin areas state `NOT BUILT / PLACEHOLDER`.
- Added Strapi 5 + PostgreSQL with editorial-only schemas and a public boundary API.
- Next.js merges Strapi editorial copy with FastAPI operational data; Strapi never owns price, stock, fitment, cart/order rules or integrations.
- Added a content-flow verifier covering draft isolation, publish/refresh, page builder, product editorial and operational-field exclusion.
- Rewrote `reports/DAVID_DEMO_SCRIPT.md` to demonstrate honest lookup behavior and CMS ownership.

